; EzyMap Scalp Mastery V2.2 BTC - EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_DIAGNOSTIC_FIRSTPASS.set
;
; ############################################################################
; #  THIS IS NOT A TRADING PROFILE. IT IS A MEASURING INSTRUMENT.            #
; #                                                                          #
; #  It is DELIBERATELY OVER-PERMISSIVE. Two filters are switched off        #
; #  outright and the lot ladder is un-halved, for one reason only: to make  #
; #  a run in which NOTHING SHOULD BE ABLE TO ZERO OUT THE TRADE COUNT.      #
; #  Its expectancy is meaningless. Do not judge the strategy by it, do not  #
; #  optimise on it, and do not put it on a live account.                    #
; ############################################################################
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Three BTCUSD.sc Strategy Tester runs at 100 / 1000 / 3000 deposit all ended:
;
;     READY=511, stored=54, deployed=0, LIVE=0
;
; 511 signals became READY, 54 were stored as persistent setups, and not one
; of the 54 ever reached the broker. Every gate between "stored" and "sent"
; is a candidate, and before V2.2 BTC S06 only ONE of them (the V2.1a
; confluence score) reported a pass/fail rate, so the journal could not
; distinguish "the spread filter rejected all 54" from "the volatility veto
; rejected all 54" from "no touch ever occurred".
;
; S06 added the missing counters. This file is the run you use to read them
; under conditions where the two most suspect filters cannot be the answer.
;
; Load this ON TOP of your V2.1b working set, on a BTCUSD or BTCUSD.sc chart,
; over the SAME period as the zero-trade runs. Every input not listed keeps
; its current value. It is EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_RECOMMENDED.set with four
; changes, all marked *** DIAGNOSTIC CHANGE *** below.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHAT TO READ AFTERWARDS
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; At OnDeinit the journal now prints:
;
;   V2.2 BTC S06 DEPLOYMENT GATE BREAKDOWN | SPREAD REJECTED: n
;     | ENVIRONMENT REJECTED: n | DAILY CAPACITY REJECTED: n
;     | ORDER-SEND ATTEMPTS: n
;   V2.2 BTC S06 DEPLOYMENT GATE BREAKDOWN BY PATH | ...
;
; Read ORDER-SEND ATTEMPTS first. If it is greater than zero the EA can
; deploy, and the zero-trade runs were caused by a FILTER you can now
; re-enable one at a time. If it is still zero with this profile loaded, no
; input in this EA is responsible - see "IF THIS STILL PRODUCES ZERO" below.
;
; EXPECTED ABSENCE: the "V2.1a CONFLUENCE FILTER RATE" line will NOT appear in
; this run. LogConfluenceFilterRate() returns early when
; InpUseConfluenceScoring is false, by design since V2.1a S01, because a rate
; of 0/0 would imply a filter that never ran had rejected everything. That is
; correct behaviour, not a missing log. The confluence line becomes readable
; again at step 3 of the retest, when scoring is switched back on. If you want
; it populated in THIS run instead, set InpUseConfluenceScoring=true and
; InpMinConfluenceScore=0.0 rather than switching the engine off - the gate
; then counts every attempt and passes every one.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; IF THIS STILL PRODUCES ZERO
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Stop tuning. With the spread gate disabled, the confluence engine off and a
; lot ladder that clears the broker minimum at 100 units, no input in this
; file can be the cause. Check the environment instead:
;
;   - No M5 history downloaded for BTCUSD.sc in the tester (the most common
;     cause by far - check the tester's own "history" tab, not the chart)
;   - Symbol not selected in Market Watch
;   - Algo trading disabled, or the tester's date range outside the data
;   - The symbol's SYMBOL_VOLUME_MIN / SYMBOL_VOLUME_STEP being something
;     unexpected - read the OnInit "BROKER-NATIVE LOT SIZING" line, which
;     prints both
;   - A deployment failure happening BEFORE these gates: read the
;     SetDeploymentFailure reasons in the journal
;
; Report the DEPLOYMENT GATE BREAKDOWN line and the OnInit block back rather
; than changing more numbers.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; *** DIAGNOSTIC CHANGE 1 of 4 - SPREAD GATE DISABLED ***
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; SpreadAllowed() opens with "if(InpMaxSpreadPoints<=0) return true;" - zero
; is an existing, documented no-op path, not a hack. Confirmed by reading the
; function in EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_ADAPTATION.mq5.
;
; This is the SINGLE MOST LIKELY cause of the zero-trade runs, and the reason
; is arithmetic rather than strategy. The gate computes
; (tick.ask-tick.bid)/_Point and compares it to InpMaxSpreadPoints=1200. On a
; BTCUSD symbol quoted with 2 digits, _Point is 0.01, so a perfectly ordinary
; $30 spread is 3000 points - two and a half times the limit, on every single
; tick, forever. RECOMMENDED.set's own section 7 already flags that 1200 is an
; unverified placeholder widened 10x from gold because the broker's point
; convention was unknown at authoring time.
;
; UPDATE (S07): a real fix landed for this instead of just a better guess -
; SpreadAllowed() can now auto-calibrate the cap from the symbol's own
; observed spread. But for THIS diagnostic pass the goal is to prove the EA
; can deploy with the spread gate fully OUT OF THE PICTURE, not to test the
; new calibration logic, so explicitly turn calibration OFF and rely on the
; existing InpMaxSpreadPoints<=0 no-op path - the same one-line, unambiguous
; "filter is completely disabled, full stop" state as before.
;
; Once this pass confirms trades occur, the NEXT test should flip
; InpAutoCalibrateSpreadCap back to true (its compiled default) - see
; RECOMMENDED.set, which leaves InpSpreadCalibrationCeilingPoints at 0
; (uncapped) on purpose, since that input used to be InpMaxSpreadPoints
; itself and a leftover 120/1200/5000 value there silently clamped the
; calibrated cap back down to whatever static number was left behind. You
; should then see "V2.2 BTC SPREAD AUTO-CALIBRATION COMPLETE" report a real
; measured cap instead of guessing another static number.
InpAutoCalibrateSpreadCap=false
InpMaxSpreadPoints=0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; *** DIAGNOSTIC CHANGE 2 of 4 - CONFLUENCE ENGINE OFF ***
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ConfluenceGateAllows() returns true immediately when this is false, before
; touching its counters and before the volatility hard-block is consulted, so
; this one switch neutralises the ENTIRE V2.1a gate - session score,
; volatility score, InpMinConfluenceScore and InpHardBlockExtremeVol together.
; ConfluenceScore() would return a neutral 1.0 pass-through even if it ran.
;
; The suspect inside this group is the volatility hard block. Its test is
; "ATR percentile < 20 OR > 90" against the same rolling window the reading
; comes from, which marks about 30% of bars extreme BY CONSTRUCTION even in a
; calm market, and clusters far worse than that on a one-directional trending
; day. As a hard veto it fired before the score was consulted and before any
; counter was incremented, so it was completely invisible in the journal.
;
; The remaining V2.1a inputs are left at RECOMMENDED values so that turning
; the engine back on at step 3 restores that profile exactly. They have no
; effect while the master switch is off. InpHardBlockExtremeVol is pinned
; false here as belt and braces.
InpUseConfluenceScoring=false
InpMinConfluenceScore=0.45
InpScoreSession=false
InpScoreVolatilityRegime=true
InpVolATRPeriod=14
InpVolTimeframe=5
InpVolPercentileLookback=500
InpVolLowPercentile=20.0
InpVolHighPercentile=90.0
InpVolatilityWeight=1.0
InpVolNormalScore=1.0
InpVolExtremeScore=0.15
InpHardBlockExtremeVol=false
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; *** DIAGNOSTIC CHANGE 3 of 4 - LOT LADDER UN-HALVED ***
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THIS IS A REAL BUG IN RECOMMENDED.set AT SMALL BALANCES, not just a
; diagnostic convenience, and it fully explains the 100-deposit run on its own.
;
; RECOMMENDED.set halves the gold ladder to InpStandardSetupLotPer100=0.005
; for BTC margin headroom. ConfidenceSetupLot() computes
; targetLot = lotPer100 * (sizingCapital / InpBaseEquity), so at a 100-unit
; deposit the STANDARD target is 0.005 * (100/100) = 0.005 lots. That is BELOW
; a 0.01 broker minimum, so NormalizeVolumeDown() returns 0.0, and because
; IsLiveCentAccount() is false in the Strategy Tester the live-cent
; minimum-lot fallback does not apply either - the function logs
; "REAL CENT SIZE BLOCK" and returns 0.0. Zero volume, no deployment.
;
; That hits the DIRECT ZERO-CONF path unconditionally, because it always calls
; ConfidenceSetupLot(0) and confidence 0 is always the STANDARD tier. GOOD
; (0.010) and QUALITY (0.015) survive at 100 units; STANDARD does not.
;
; NOTE that InpForceMinimumBaseSizing does NOT rescue this. The floor raises
; the sizing CAPITAL to 100, and at a 100-unit deposit it already was 100 -
; the shortfall is in the per-100 lot RATE, not in the capital. This is worth
; being explicit about because it is exactly the case the floor was requested
; for and exactly the case it cannot fix.
;
; The unhalved ladder below is gold's, and gives 0.01 at 100 units - the
; broker minimum, which is what a 100-unit account should be trading anyway.
; If you go back to the halved ladder, use at least a 200-unit deposit.
InpBaseEquity=100.0
InpBaseLayerLot=0.01
InpStandardSetupLotPer100=0.01
InpGoodSetupLotPer100=0.02
InpQualitySetupLotPer100=0.03
InpForceMinimumBaseSizing=true
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; *** DIAGNOSTIC CHANGE 4 of 4 - RISK GUARD WIDENED ***
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CapVolumeForStandardRiskGuard() blocks outright when even the broker minimum
; lot would risk more than this percentage of equity, logging
; "STANDARD RISK GUARD BLOCK". On BTC with a 210-pip (= $210) stop, one 0.01
; lot risks about $2.10, which is 2.1% of a 100-unit account - inside the
; compiled default of 5.0%, but not by much, and the ATR-resolved stop can run
; wider than the 210-pip preset. RECOMMENDED.set does not set this input at
; all, so it runs at that 5.0% default. Widened here so it cannot be the thing
; that zeroes the run. REMOVE THIS LINE (OR SET IT BACK TO 5.0) BEFORE ANY
; REAL TEST - it is the one change in this file that genuinely increases risk,
; and unlike the other three it is not part of the RECOMMENDED profile.
InpConfidenceLotRiskGuardPct=25.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; EVERYTHING BELOW IS UNCHANGED FROM RECOMMENDED.set
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Reproduced in full so this file is self-contained and so the geometry the
; EA trades is the geometry you are actually trying to diagnose. See
; EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_RECOMMENDED.set for the reasoning behind every number;
; all of it still applies, and all of it is still UNVALIDATED against real BTC
; data.
;
; ATR geometry - ON. Self-relative, so it transfers to BTC. Multipliers are
; gold's tuned dimensionless ratios; only the pip-denominated floor/ceiling
; are rescaled x10.
InpUseATRGeometry=true
InpATRPeriod=14
InpATRTimeframe=5
InpATRStopMultiplier=1.60
InpATRTrailMultiplier=0.55
InpATRArmMultiplier=0.35
InpATRStopFloorPips=120.0
InpATRStopCeilingPips=350.0
InpATRTrailFloorPips=50.0
;
; Stop / trail / breakeven. Some are superseded at runtime by ATR geometry,
; some are only rescaled by it, some are never touched by it.
InpPresetStopLossPips=210.0
InpTrailArmPips=70.0
InpTrailInitialDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailTightenAtPips=999.0
InpTrailTightDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailingActivationPips=0.0
InpTrailingDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailingStepPips=10.0
InpBreakevenLockAtPips=90.0
InpBreakevenLockOffsetPips=10.0
;
; Partial TP.
InpPartialTPPips=110.0
InpGradeAPartialTPPips=160.0
InpGradeBPartialTPPips=110.0
InpGradeCPartialTPPips=70.0
;
; Tolerances and zone geometry - live regardless of ATR geometry.
InpEntryTouchTolerancePips=50.0
InpZeroConfTouchTolerancePips=90.0
InpZeroConfClusterTolerancePips=90.0
InpConfluenceTolerancePips=700.0
InpZoneIdentityTolerancePips=80.0
InpM1ZoneTolerancePips=80.0
InpSnrFrontRunPips=100.0
InpLimitZoneDuplicateTolerancePips=10.0
InpLiveLimitGeometryExtensionPips=200.0
InpTouchStallMaxExtendPips=20.0
;
; Mode stop/target scaffolding - feeds RR planning and PersistentFallbackSL().
InpScalpStopPips=200.0
InpIntradayStopPips=350.0
InpSwingStopPips=700.0
InpScalpTargetMinPoints=150.0
InpScalpTargetMaxPoints=800.0
InpIntradayTargetMinPoints=600.0
InpIntradayTargetMaxPoints=2500.0
InpSwingTargetMinPoints=1800.0
InpSwingTargetMaxPoints=8000.0
;
; Distal stops - only consumed when InpUseZoneDistalStops is true, which is
; not enabled here.
InpDistalStopBufferPips=30.0
InpDistalStopMinPips=100.0
InpDistalStopMaxPips=300.0
;
; Round-number grading tolerance - only consumed when InpUseZoneGrading is
; true, which is not enabled here.
InpRoundNumberTolerancePips=50.0
;
; Higher-timeframe level separation floors (V2.2 BTC S03).
InpH4LevelMinDistancePips=700.0
InpD1LevelMinDistancePips=1200.0
InpW1LevelMinDistancePips=2000.0
InpH1LevelMinDistancePips=700.0
;
; Slippage. Unchanged; only the spread gate above was disabled.
InpDeviationPoints=200
;
; Magic number - distinct from the XAUUSD default so the journal is readable.
InpMagicNumber=2475222
